(1522, 'ScreenDocs Expanded 2016 - Jakarta', 'screendocs-expanded-2016-jakarta-3', 'Lainnya', 'FILM SCREENING | MASTER CLASSES | DISCUSSIONS | VR
Erasmus Huis | Institut Français d''Indonésie
ALL EVENTS ARE FREE AND OPEN FOR PUBLIC

ScreenDocs Expanded is In-Docs’ film literacy program that showcases inspiring international and Indonesian documentaries. This program is intended to build documentary audience and to encourage critical thinking among young audience, through exposure to diverse perspectives.

The event will take place in Jakarta from 1-4 December 2016 at Erasmus Huis and Institut Français d''Indonésie (IFI). Thirty international and Indonesian documentaries will be exhibited during four days of documentary film festival filled with screenings, discussions, and master classes by world documentary experts.

